        "original_id": "d4993c5a-29a0-501a-a821-48657a124cb5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: The Lost Tomb of Jesus documentary, 1980 Jerusalem ossuary discovery\n- People: Jesus, Mary Magdalene, Judah\n- Concepts: ossuaries, secondary burial\n- Places: Jerusalem\n\nFacts:\n- In 1980, ossuaries were discovered in Jerusalem.\n- The 2007 documentary \"The Lost Tomb of Jesus\" proposed that inscriptions on the Jerusalem ossuaries were evidence that Jesus was married to Mary Magdalene and that they had a son named Judah.\n- An ossuary is a chest, box, building, well, or site used as the final resting place of human skeletal remains.\n- In secondary burial, a body is first buried in a temporary grave, and after some years the skeletal remains are removed and placed in an ossuary.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
